# === geometry — candidates bind the Cl(12)/E8/4096-d substrate ================ #
ex:ecGeometryWrongCarrierDim a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/geometry-wrong-carrier-dim.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:GeometricBindingConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A candidate's gmeow:candidateGeometry math:CliffordAlgebra has math:spaceDimension 2048 instead of 4096 = 2^12; the signature is a valid (11, 1) so the p + q = 12 arm holds, isolating the carrier-dimension arm. The ∀→(¬∃ signature-mismatch ∧ ¬∃ dimension-mismatch) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:GeometricBindingConstraint (gmeow:GeometryDimensionMismatch) MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:GeometricBindingConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The math:MetricSignature carries no metric-tensor / manifold chain, so the grounding math:MetricSignatureDimensionConstraint's guard never fires — the preference Cl(12)/4096-d gate is the sole violation. The cell does NOT claim gmeow:expectedSoleFinding, and the reason is not the fixture: EVERY preference conformance run also reports the two standing loss-ledger findings described in the header note, so no counter-example in this slice can be sole." .

# === AC6 — promotion grants no activation; activation needs a held gate ======= #
ex:ecPromotionGrantsActivation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/promotion-grants-activation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:PromotionNotActivationConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A gmeow:PromotionReceipt carries a gmeow:grantsActivation edge — forbidden, because promotion recommends and never activates. The activation is properly gmeow:activationAuthorizedBy a held gmeow:ConsumerImprovementGate, so gmeow:ActivationAuthorityConstraint is SATISFIED and not the violation under test; the sole defect is the grant on a promotion receipt, so the forbidden-pattern SPARQL constraint of gmeow:PromotionNotActivationConstraint (AC6) MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:PromotionNotActivationConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The cell does NOT claim gmeow:expectedSoleFinding, and the reason is not the fixture: EVERY preference conformance run also reports the two standing loss-ledger findings described in the header note, so no counter-example in this slice can be sole." .

# === AC4 — DPO is a derived-only consumer, never the canonical source ========= #
ex:ecDpoAsCanonical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/dpo-as-canonical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:DpoNotCanonicalConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A gmeow:DpoView carries the forbidden gmeow:derivesCanonicalObservation edge, sourcing a canonical gmeow:PreferenceObservation from the training view and inverting the canonical→projection direction. The DpoView is otherwise a well-formed projection receipt and the observation carries its mandatory gmeow:comparisonContext and observed feature, so the forbidden-pattern SPARQL constraint of gmeow:DpoNotCanonicalConstraint (AC4) MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:DpoNotCanonicalConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The cell does NOT claim gmeow:expectedSoleFinding, and the reason is not the fixture: EVERY preference conformance run also reports the two standing loss-ledger findings described in the header note, so no counter-example in this slice can be sole." .
